<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hrvoje Vukčić Hrvatinić</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1350–<a href="/years/1416">1416</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hrvoje Vukčić Hrvatinić was the most powerful Bosnian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnate</a> of his day, who made and unmade Bosnian kings after the death of Tvrtko I. Backing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ladislaus-of-naples">Ladislaus of Naples</a> against Sigismund for the Hungarian crown, he received the title Duke of Split and the central Dalmatian islands in 1403. His missal, the Hrvoje Missal, is a celebrated Glagolitic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hrvoje-vukcic-hrvatinic.jpg" alt="Hrvoje Vukčić Hrvatinić" width="237" height="293" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: scribe Butko · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hrvoje_Vukcic_Hrvatinic_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
